<p>
	Every setting can be overridden for a project and its subprojects with a
	<%= link_to "project custom field", new_custom_field_path(:type => "ProjectCustomField") %>
	named "Google Chat" and the setting name without "?", e.g. "Google Chat Post Issue Updates":
	a boolean field for the yes/no settings, a long text field for "Ignored Fields" and a text field for the others.
	Empty values use the setting of the parent project or of the plugin.
</p>

<p>
	<%= label_tag 'settings[hangouts_chat_url]', 'Google Chat URL' %>
	<%= text_field_tag 'settings[hangouts_chat_url]', settings['hangouts_chat_url'], :size => 80 %>
	<em class="info">Webhook URL of the Google Chat space.</em>
</p>

<p>
	<%= label_tag 'settings[thread]', 'Google Chat Thread' %>
	<%= text_field_tag 'settings[thread]', settings['thread'] %>
	<em class="info">
		Without a thread, every message is posted on its own.
		The thread "-" disables the messages; in a project, not those of its subprojects.
	</em>
</p>

<p>
	<%= label_tag 'settings[thread_per_issue]', 'One Thread per Issue?' %>
	<%= check_box_tag 'settings[thread_per_issue]', '1', settings['thread_per_issue'] == '1' %>
	<em class="info">
		Posts all messages about an issue to the thread "&lt;thread&gt;-issue-&lt;id&gt;", or "redmine-issue-&lt;id&gt;" without a thread.
		Wiki updates stay in the thread.
	</em>
</p>

<p>
	<%= label_tag 'settings[display_watchers]', 'Display Watchers?' %>
	<%= select_tag 'settings[display_watchers]', options_for_select([['Yes', 'yes'], ['No', 'no']], settings['display_watchers'] == 'yes' ? 'yes' : 'no') %>
	<em class="info">Lists the watchers in messages about new issues.</em>
</p>

<p>
	<%= label_tag 'settings[post_description]', 'Post Description?' %>
	<%= check_box_tag 'settings[post_description]', '1', settings['post_description'] == '1' %>
	<em class="info">Posts the description of a new issue as the first reply to its message.</em>
</p>

<p>
	<%= label_tag 'settings[post_updates]', 'Post Issue Updates?' %>
	<%= check_box_tag 'settings[post_updates]', '1', settings['post_updates'] == '1' %>
	<em class="info">Posts changes of issues with their changed fields and notes. New issues are always posted.</em>
</p>

<p>
	<%= label_tag 'settings[post_wiki_updates]', 'Post Wiki Updates?' %>
	<%= check_box_tag 'settings[post_wiki_updates]', '1', settings['post_wiki_updates'] == '1' %>
	<em class="info">Posts changes of wiki pages with their comment.</em>
</p>

<p>
	<%= label_tag 'settings[ignored_fields]', 'Ignored Fields' %>
	<%= text_area_tag 'settings[ignored_fields]', settings['ignored_fields'], :rows => 4, :cols => 40 %>
	<em class="info">
		Changes to these fields are not posted, one field per line. Use the name of a custom field or of an issue attribute.
		Updates which only change ignored fields and have no notes are not sent at all.
	</em>
</p>

<p>
	<%= label_tag 'settings[order_approval]', 'Order Approval?' %>
	<%= check_box_tag 'settings[order_approval]', '1', settings['order_approval'] == '1' %>
	<em class="info">Issues whose subject contains "Bestellung" get a button to approve them, and chat messages about them a "Freigeben" button.</em>
</p>
